{ "ndm_detectspikes", "thresholdNoise", "stderiv", "Optional", false,
  "stderiv engine only: the signal the baseline noise sigma is measured on. sdiff (default, historical) measures the spatial derivative BEFORE the temporal first-difference, but detection thresholds the differenced signal, whose noise is smaller -- so the threshold sits higher than thresholdFactor * 4 sigma (about 1.65x on the reference session: 0.8 gives ~5.3 sigma). stderiv measures the detection signal itself, so the threshold is exactly thresholdFactor * 4 sigma; re-pick thresholdFactor when switching (~1.33 reproduces the historical 0.8). The run log prints the effective threshold in detection-signal sigma for either choice." },
{ "ndm_detectspikes", "recenterMode", "raw", "Optional", false,
  "stderiv engine only: where each detection is placed before the shared .res is written. stderiv (default, historical) = sample of maximum summed |stderiv| over the group. raw = sample of maximum negative deflection of the group-referenced raw signal (x - group mean), summed over the group in per-channel noise units -- the physical trough; stable for units whose stderiv waveform has several near-equal extrema. Applied to every spike (mixing anchors within a unit splits it into two alignments). With raw, the stderiv waveforms extracted later carry their extremum a few samples before peakSampleIndex." },
{ "ndm_detectspikes", "recenterHalfWidth", "8", "Optional", false,
  "stderiv engine only: search +-recenterHalfWidth samples around each detection (0 = no re-centring). Unset keeps the historical window [-(peakSampleIndex-1), peakSearchLength-peakSampleIndex], which can move a detection onto a neighbouring spike. recenterMode raw with 8 was the best tested setting on the reference session." },
{ "ndm_detectspikes", "detectArms", "hybrid", "Optional", false,
  "stderiv engine only: stderiv (default) detects on the stderiv signal alone. hybrid adds a second detection pass on the group-referenced raw signal (x - group mean, no temporal difference) and merges the two with the refractory rule. Each pass thresholds at thresholdFactor * 4 sigma of its OWN signal (implies thresholdNoise stderiv; an explicit sdiff is refused). Recovers spikes the spatial derivative attenuates (footprints shared by neighbouring channels), at the cost of admitting more multi-unit activity. Use with recenterHalfWidth below refractoryPeriod/2 so merged events cannot be re-centred onto one sample. The .res keeps the method name (stderiv); the run log records the arms and per-arm counts." },
{ "ndm_detectspikes", "flatRunMax", "5", "Optional", false,
  "stderiv engine only: reject a spike whose raw window has more than flatRunMax identical consecutive samples on any channel (zero-filled gaps, stuck lines). 0 or unset = off. The median high-pass (ndm_hipass) leaves short exact-zero runs (up to ~17 samples) that make 5 remove 31% of spikes on the reference chunk; ~20 keeps them and still catches dropouts." },
