{ "ndm_extractspikes", "flatRunMax", "5", "Optional", false,
  "Drop spikes with more than flatRunMax identical consecutive samples on any channel, checked in the RAW source window (inputExtension, e.g. .fil) at the spike time AND in the freshly extracted waveform. The raw check is what finds a dropped-out channel, zero fill or a stuck line: a spatial derivative mixes a dead channel with its live neighbours, so it is not flat in a stderiv/sdiff .spk. The median high-pass (ndm_hipass) leaves short exact-zero runs (up to ~17 samples); a threshold of ~20 separates channel dropouts from those. 0 or unset = off." },
{ "ndm_extractspikes", "dedupSamples", "0", "Optional", false,
